WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.167
-Donald Trump Jr.
took the stand

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:04.300
in the ongoing
New York fraud trial

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.701
against his family's business

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:07.434
and claimed that he had
virtually nothing to do

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:09.267
with his own company's
financial documents,

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:10.767
even though he personally
signed them.

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:12.767
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:14.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:16.901
♪♪

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:19.634
Even as Donald Trump remains
the overwhelming favorite to win

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:22.334
the GOP nomination
for president in 2024,

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:23.734
he and his various underlings

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:26.501
are finally starting to face
legal and financial consequences

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:28.534
for their attempt to overturn
the 2020 election,

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:30.200
like his ex-lawyer
Sidney Powell,

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.100
the insane leopard-print lady

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.734
who stood in front
of a soaking-wet Rudy Giuliani

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:38.300
and claimed China, Cuba,
and the ghost of Hugo Chavez

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.601
had all teamed up with
an election software company

00:00:40.601 --> 00:00:43.234
to rig voting machines,
and then was later a key witness

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:45.834
in the January 6th
congressional investigation,

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:47.834
where she showed up
to her deposition

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:51.234
chugging Diet Dr. Pepper
like it was Pepto-Bismol

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:53.901
and looking like Grandma Saracen
from "Friday Night Lights."

00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:55.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.467
"Hey, Grandma, I'm gonna
go study with Julie, okay?"

00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:00.267
"Matt, lock the door behind you.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:03.367
I don't want Hugo Chavez
to get me."

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:06.400
"All right, I'll stay.
I hope Julie doesn't get mad."

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.734
And, yeah, that --
maybe you're thinking

00:01:09.734 --> 00:01:11.434
that "Friday Night Lights"
reference

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:12.634
would've worked better
when it aired,

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:14.234
but not a lot of people
watched it then.

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:16.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:17.968
I don't think it was ever
gonna work.

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:20.934
But if it makes one more person

00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:23.501
start "Friday Night Lights,"
it was worth it.

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:25.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.467
Well, Powell has now
pleaded guilty in Georgia,

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:28.634
and as part
of her guilty plea,

00:01:28.634 --> 00:01:30.234
she agreed to cooperate
with prosecutors

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:33.234
and pay restitution to
the secretary of state's office,

00:01:33.234 --> 00:01:35.601
as well as an additional fine.
And on Wednesday,

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:37.367
one of Georgia's senior
election officials,

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:39.634
a Republican,
showed off the check

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:41.434
she wrote to
the secretary of state's office

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:44.000
at a press conference
to discuss election integrity.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.400
-For over three years now,

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:51.033
we have had people lying about
our elections in Georgia.

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:52.567
We have now begun to see
the accountability

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:53.868
of that take place.

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:58.167
So yesterday afternoon,
we received

00:01:58.167 --> 00:02:02.601
our first restitution check
from Sidney Powell.

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:05.567
It's a small down payment
on which we owe to the voters

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:09.234
and the people of Georgia.
It's $2,700.

00:02:09.234 --> 00:02:11.601
-Huh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:12.968
Just $2,700?

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:16.400
Is that worth
a press conference?

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.067
I feel like holding
a press conference

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:20.033
might cost more than $2,700.

00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:22.033
But you know what?
It's your money, Georgia.

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:23.634
You go crazy.
Still, knowing Sidney Powell,

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:27.801
$2,700 could be all of her
Diet Dr. Pepper money.

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:29.868
Now she's gonna have
to downgrade to Mr. Pibb.

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:34.200
"I could never imbibe
such an anti-American beverage.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.467
Mr. Pibb, as we all know,
colluded with Mr. Peanut

00:02:37.467 --> 00:02:41.133
and the ghost of Chester Cheetah
to steal our elections.

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:44.734
That's why I had no choice but
to kill him and wear his pelt

00:02:44.734 --> 00:02:47.434
as my sweater."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:49.334
So, multiple Trump associates,
including Powell,

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:51.167
have already flipped
and pleaded guilty in Georgia,

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:53.634
an actual criminal case that
could put Trump behind bars.

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:56.534
And yet, it's the civil fraud
trial in Manhattan

00:02:56.534 --> 00:02:57.767
that seems to have
rattled him the most.

00:02:57.767 --> 00:02:58.801
According to
The Washington Post...

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:13.534
First of all, how can you tell
when he's livid?

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:15.934
Because he always looks livid.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.934 --> 00:03:18.100
He has resting livid face.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:21.367
He scowls more than
an apartment cat

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:24.400
watching dogs pass
by through the window.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.000
Second, I buy the line
about his brand,

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.367
but not the line about
his children's inheritance.

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:32.334
There is no way Trump plans
on leaving his children

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:35.300
with anything other than
a giant stack of unpaid bills.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:37.200
If he has any money left
when he dies,

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.667
he's going to be entombed
with it like a pharaoh.

00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:42.767
[ As Trump ]
"Bury me with my last $300

00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:44.501
and also Rudy Giuliani."

00:03:44.501 --> 00:03:46.534
[ As Giuliani ]
"It'll be an honor, boss.

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:48.601
You want to be big spoon
or little spoon?"

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:49.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:51.033
[ As Trump ]
"I want you to stay alive

00:03:51.033 --> 00:03:55.601
and scare the rats away
from my dead body."

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:57.334
[ As Giuliani ]
"The dream!"

00:03:57.334 --> 00:04:01.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.200
[ Normal voice ] What really
seems to be pissing Trump off

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.601
is the judge in the case

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:06.934
ruling that he's just not as
wealthy as he claims to be.

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:08.434
For example,
Trump has been furious

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:10.934
about the judge's valuation
of his Mar-a-Lago estate,

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:14.300
which Trump claims
is worth more than $1 billion.

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.200
-I have a house
that's very valuable,

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:21.067
and they try and make it like
I'm increasing values.

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:23.734
And, honestly,
it's a very conservative number.

00:04:23.734 --> 00:04:26.467
But they valued a house
that's worth 100 times

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:28.200
more than the number they used.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.634
Let's say 50 to 100.

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:32.767
They valued it at $18 million,

00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:35.334
and people say it's worth
anywhere from 50 to 100

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:37.200
and maybe even that more.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.133
He's been given
this information.

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:41.534
It's now been proven
to be false,

00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:43.767
such as Mar-a-Lago
in Palm Beach, Florida,

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:46.501
being worth $18 million,

00:04:46.501 --> 00:04:50.100
when, in fact, it's much closer
to $1.5 billion.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.834
-1.5 billion?

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:56.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.501 --> 00:04:59.067
You're saying
your low-rent SeaWorld rip-off,

00:04:59.067 --> 00:05:00.734
a chintzy roadside motel

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:02.934
that looks like the kind
of thing state health inspectors

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:04.767
would shut down
because they found feces on

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:08.033
the Slip 'N Slide is worth as
much as the Burj Khalifa?

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:12.934
Your dumb hotel for plastic
surgeons and their third wives

00:05:12.934 --> 00:05:14.801
is worth $1 billion?

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:16.934
It looks like
the fake-stucco castle

00:05:16.934 --> 00:05:19.601
on the 13th hole
of a miniature-golf course.

00:05:19.601 --> 00:05:23.067
Not even the 18th,
that [bleep] 5-foot-high castle

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:26.234
where you could see
the chicken wire sticking out.

00:05:26.234 --> 00:05:27.968
But if you're still skeptical
about Trump's claim

00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:29.367
that his crappy aquarium
is worth

00:05:29.367 --> 00:05:30.734
a billion and a half dollars,
don't worry.

00:05:30.734 --> 00:05:32.167
He's got a crack investigator --

00:05:32.167 --> 00:05:36.200
I'm sorry, an investigator
who's head cracked on the case.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.100
Rudy Giuliani
did some solid research

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.934
to prove that Trump's financial
assessment is accurate.

00:05:40.934 --> 00:05:43.467
-So, I'm down in Mar-a-Lago,
and, yesterday, I went out

00:05:43.467 --> 00:05:47.133
and I did some shopping,
house shopping.

00:05:47.133 --> 00:05:52.000
And I found, in about one hour,
seven pieces of property,

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:56.000
none of them 1/20
the size of Mar-a-Lago,

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.767
for over $25 million.

00:05:58.767 --> 00:06:00.501
-That's right -- Rudy claims he
went out and did some

00:06:00.501 --> 00:06:03.267
house shopping, which definitely
means multiple people in Florida

00:06:03.267 --> 00:06:05.033
were calling the police
and saying, "Hi.

00:06:05.033 --> 00:06:07.200
I'm not sure if this qualifies
as an emergency,

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.133
but a very strange man
in what are either short pants

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:14.901
or long shorts
just asked to buy our house."

00:06:14.901 --> 00:06:18.167
Of course, when Rudy says
he went house shopping,

00:06:18.167 --> 00:06:20.567
that means there's a good chance
he went to the Waffle House.

00:06:20.567 --> 00:06:24.701
"The All-Star Special alone
is worth at least $10 million."

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:26.601
Rudy then went on to
claim that --

00:06:26.601 --> 00:06:28.501
He even showed
a specific example

00:06:28.501 --> 00:06:31.234
of one such house on his
so-called live cast.

00:06:31.234 --> 00:06:34.868
-And I put them on my live cast
last night.

00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:38.300
I put one particular
one on that

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:46.701
the whole house is about half
the size of the main house.

00:06:46.701 --> 00:06:49.767
Don't count in all the
other houses, the beach house.

00:06:49.767 --> 00:06:54.634
And, by the way, this house
is four blocks from the ocean

00:06:54.634 --> 00:06:56.501
and three blocks
from the Intracoastal.

00:06:56.501 --> 00:06:58.567
And, of course,
Mar-a-Lago is on both.

00:06:58.567 --> 00:07:01.601
-One, it's very strange
to wear a tuxedo shirt

00:07:01.601 --> 00:07:03.267
without the rest of the tuxedo.

00:07:03.267 --> 00:07:07.567
[ Laughter ]

00:07:07.567 --> 00:07:08.934
The whole time you're
watching it,

00:07:08.934 --> 00:07:11.067
you're like, "Are you getting
home from a party

00:07:11.067 --> 00:07:13.467
or are you going to a party?

00:07:13.467 --> 00:07:17.267
Whose parties do you go to?"

00:07:17.267 --> 00:07:20.100
Two, Rudy would make
a terrible real-estate agent.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:21.434
The whole time he was talking,

00:07:21.434 --> 00:07:23.234
I had no clue what the hell
he's talking about.

00:07:23.234 --> 00:07:24.534
"I found a great place.

00:07:24.534 --> 00:07:26.567
The whole size is half
the house of the main house,

00:07:26.567 --> 00:07:27.901
and it's four blocks
from the beach

00:07:27.901 --> 00:07:29.367
and three blocks
from the Intracoastal.

00:07:29.367 --> 00:07:31.434
There's 10 bathrooms,
if you count closets,

00:07:31.434 --> 00:07:33.067
and no closets, because, well,

00:07:33.067 --> 00:07:35.367
you will not want
to go in there."

00:07:35.367 --> 00:07:38.701
[ Laughter ]

00:07:38.701 --> 00:07:40.133
"Now, if you'll excuse me,

00:07:40.133 --> 00:07:43.934
I either have to put on this bow
tie or take off these pants."

00:07:46.567 --> 00:07:49.100
Surpri...
[ Laughter ]

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:51.834
Surprisingly, Rudy's research
has not solved the case,

00:07:51.834 --> 00:07:53.400
and, on Wednesday,
Trump's eldest son,

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:54.634
Don Jr., was called to testify.

00:07:54.634 --> 00:07:55.934
At first, he seemed
to be enjoying

00:07:55.934 --> 00:07:57.200
all the attention
from the cameras

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:58.734
while he sat
at the defense table.

00:07:58.734 --> 00:08:00.801
[ Camera shutters clicking ]

00:08:04.467 --> 00:08:06.167
-I should have worn makeup.

00:08:10.334 --> 00:08:12.601
-Needing makeup
is such a TV insider joke.

00:08:12.601 --> 00:08:14.400
Like, most people don't know
what you're talking about.

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:16.067
I get it because I work in TV.

00:08:16.067 --> 00:08:18.167
I have to wear makeup
whenever I'm on camera,

00:08:18.167 --> 00:08:20.534
a fact that I took for granted
until I filmed my show

00:08:20.534 --> 00:08:23.067
from home during COVID
and had to do my own makeup

00:08:23.067 --> 00:08:26.467
and looked like
I was haunting my own house.

00:08:26.467 --> 00:08:30.968
I looked healthier
when I actually had COVID.

00:08:30.968 --> 00:08:33.367
[ Laughter ]

00:08:33.367 --> 00:08:36.167
But then when it came time
to actually answer questions,

00:08:36.167 --> 00:08:38.033
Don Jr. seemed
much less forthcoming,

00:08:38.033 --> 00:08:39.567
even claiming
he had no involvement

00:08:39.567 --> 00:08:42.200
in preparing financial documents
that he personally signed.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.868
-Donald Trump Jr. took the stand
late this afternoon,

00:08:44.868 --> 00:08:48.033
and he denied having any
involvement in the preparation

00:08:48.033 --> 00:08:49.968
of the financial statements
in this case.

00:08:49.968 --> 00:08:51.267
These are the same statements

00:08:51.267 --> 00:08:53.734
the judge has already found
to be fraudulent.

00:08:53.734 --> 00:08:56.801
So Trump was asked specifically
about this, his role,

00:08:56.801 --> 00:08:58.534
if he had any involvement
in the preparation.

00:08:58.534 --> 00:09:01.567
He said, "I did not.
The accountants worked on that.

00:09:01.567 --> 00:09:02.934
That's what we pay them for."

00:09:02.934 --> 00:09:05.601
Now, he was specifically
asked about 2017.

00:09:05.601 --> 00:09:08.167
That's the year
that he became the trustee

00:09:08.167 --> 00:09:10.834
of his father's trust
when he became president.

00:09:10.834 --> 00:09:12.667
And that's the first time
that Donald Trump Jr.

00:09:12.667 --> 00:09:15.367
signed the statement certifying
that they were accurate.

00:09:15.367 --> 00:09:18.834
Now, Trump Jr. testified that
he may have provided information

00:09:18.834 --> 00:09:20.334
to the internal accountants

00:09:20.334 --> 00:09:21.968
who were working
on these statements,

00:09:21.968 --> 00:09:24.434
but he said he didn't know
that what he gave them

00:09:24.434 --> 00:09:26.868
would be used
in the financial statements.

00:09:26.868 --> 00:09:29.100
-I'm sorry. His testimony
is that he had nothing to do

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:30.467
with the financial statements,

00:09:30.467 --> 00:09:32.634
except when he gave information
to the accountants

00:09:32.634 --> 00:09:35.067
preparing those
financial statements,

00:09:35.067 --> 00:09:37.234
but he didn't think they would
use that information

00:09:37.234 --> 00:09:39.634
in the statements
they were preparing.

00:09:39.634 --> 00:09:40.868
That's like one of my writers,

00:09:40.868 --> 00:09:43.067
after a joke of theirs bombs
in the monologue,

00:09:43.067 --> 00:09:47.000
telling me, "I didn't think
you were gonna use it!"

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:50.901
And, by the way, that happens
all the [bleep] time!

00:09:50.901 --> 00:09:54.367
The amount they blame me!
"Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:09:54.367 --> 00:09:57.801
Those aren't
for public consumption!"

00:09:57.801 --> 00:10:00.300
Also, Don Jr. admits
he signed the statement

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:01.801
certifying they were accurate.

00:10:01.801 --> 00:10:03.767
You don't get to claim
you didn't know what was in it

00:10:03.767 --> 00:10:05.067
and then just walk away
scot free.

00:10:05.067 --> 00:10:06.334
That doesn't work
for anyone else.

00:10:06.334 --> 00:10:07.767
That would be like
John Hancock saying,

00:10:07.767 --> 00:10:11.834
"Independence from England?
I never agreed to that."

00:10:11.834 --> 00:10:13.968
If I so much
as check the wrong box

00:10:13.968 --> 00:10:15.200
when I sign up for cable,

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:18.434
I end up with a recurring charge
of $39.99 a month

00:10:18.434 --> 00:10:20.734
for something called
NFL End Zone +,

00:10:20.734 --> 00:10:23.200
which is just a webcam
on empty stadiums

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:25.667
when their home team
is playing somewhere else.

00:10:25.667 --> 00:10:27.868
The only people who subscribe
to it are Giants fans

00:10:27.868 --> 00:10:30.601
because it's their only chance
to see the end zone.

00:10:30.601 --> 00:10:31.901
[ Laughter ]

00:10:31.901 --> 00:10:35.534
"Oh, oh! Look! It has
blue grass! That's so cool!

00:10:35.534 --> 00:10:38.601
I can see why our team doesn't
ever want to step on it."

00:10:38.601 --> 00:10:41.400
[ Laughter ]

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:43.267
Trump is facing four
separate criminal cases

00:10:43.267 --> 00:10:44.968
and, on top of that,
a civil fraud case

00:10:44.968 --> 00:10:46.234
that could topple his business

00:10:46.234 --> 00:10:47.667
and destroy
his personal mythology.

00:10:47.667 --> 00:10:49.400
He spent decades
claiming he's a billionaire,

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:50.901
but as this trial has proven,

00:10:50.901 --> 00:10:52.767
his net worth
is much closer to...

00:10:52.767 --> 00:10:54.934
-$2,700.

00:10:54.934 --> 00:10:56.167
-This has been...

00:10:56.167 --> 00:10:58.534
You're back!
You're back, Sally!

00:10:58.534 --> 00:11:00.200
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:03.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:03.567 --> 00:11:05.834
Hey, everybody. Thanks
for watching "A Closer Look."

00:11:05.834 --> 00:11:07.767
And as a reminder,
